  "worked_solution": "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=4{y}^{3}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}=\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(4{y}^{3})=0\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)+8.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)+8)=0=\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)+8$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1)-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1)-3)=0=\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1)-3$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=2x+7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(2x+7)=0=\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2x+7$ gives an exact equation.",
